sched: provide mark_reserved() in the !SCHED_WALT branch

fair.c calls mark_reserved() from unguarded paths (load_balance and
check_for_migration); the !SCHED_WALT branch of kernel/sched/sched.h
declares is_reserved() and clear_reserved() only. Add the matching
no-op stub so WALT-disabled 4.9 builds compile.

diff --git a/kernel/sched/sched.h b/kernel/sched/sched.h
index a9db959..023d692 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/sched.h
+++ b/kernel/sched/sched.h
@@ -2935,6 +2935,11 @@ static inline int is_reserved(int cpu)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static inline int mark_reserved(int cpu)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static inline int got_boost_kick(void)
 {
 	return 0;
